<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-52) maps every implemented equation to its source and lists the Lean file; the Section 2b header (L480-522) states the PCP/hinge model equation by equation with citations and an explicit not-modelled list; function docstrings cite Farhadifar Eq. 1 derivatives, Etournay's |Q| = 1/2 ln(a/b), Classen/Aigouy for the Fz-Stbm bridge; the math_kg YAML registers both new theorems with code loci (L50-86). Deductions: the gains k_fb = 0.6, k_flow = 0.4, polarity noise 0.02, initial spread 0.6 rad, T1 lengths 0.08/0.12 and the |Q|/0.15 saturation are stated but not traced to any source (-6); the Section 2 reweighting at L401-405 and the hex pull at L378-379 carry comments that cite Farhadifar p. 2101 / Classen 2005 for steps those papers do not contain (-6)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py L376–L379: Comment attributes the hexagonal-lattice pull to Classen 2005 / Farhadifar 2007 p. 2101, which describe PCP-driven remodeling, not a lattice-restoring force <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py#L376-L379>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: Farhadifar Eq. 1-2 single-cell energy and the Case I/II/III ground-state classifier (L120-202), the ablation recoil model (L205-234), and in Pass 3 a true vertex model — mesh built from the Voronoi tessellation with CCW rings and 3-valent interior vertices (L533-567), per-bond Fz/Stbm asymmetry tensor c_ab/a_ab = n.Q_ab.n (L617-647), analytic forces dA/dr, dL/dr, dl/dr with half-shared bond tension (L650-692) that pass a central-difference check to 1e-5 (self-test 10, L1912-1927), T1 exchange with 4-cell re-wiring (L723-771), hinge-contraction pure shear and polarity dynamics (L846-935). Deductions: panels A1-A4 and measurements 1-7 still come from the Section 2 Voronoi-seed Lloyd relaxation, whose Lewis's-law agreement is produced by an explicit post-hoc reweighting `adjusted_areas = areas * (1 + 0.14 * gamma_slope_boost * (n - 6))` (L401-405) and whose pupal regime is pulled toward the perfect lattice by `0.042 * hex_disp` (L378-379) — neither is in Farhadifar et al. (2007) (-8); the explicit vertex model is a clamped non-periodic patch, so boundary cells are prescribed rather than mechanically coupled, and the PCP coupling sign, k_fb, k_flow and the |Q|/0.15 saturation (L931) are uncited modelling choices (-5); polarity is polar but the tension law is nematic, so Fz-distal vs Stbm-proximal identity does not enter the mechanics beyond the bridge density (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py L378–L379: Pupal regime adds 0.042 * displacement toward the perfect hexagonal lattice (seeds_hex) — hexagonal order is partly imposed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py#L378-L379>",
        "2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py L401–L405: Post-hoc area reweighting by (n - 6) in the Section 2 regimes imposes Lewis's law rather than deriving it from the energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py#L401-L405>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 14 measurements with units and reference values (L1723-1845): the 8 Pass 2 metrics are unchanged (wing P(6) = 0.440 vs 0.455, pupal 0.840 vs 0.78, Lewis r = 0.9994, specimen r = 0.9913, recoil v0 = 0.22 um/s) and 6 Pass 3 metrics are added — elongation peak <|Q|> = 0.253 vs ~0.25, rearrangement share 0.307 vs ~0.5, oriented-T1 fraction 1.00 vs the 0.5 isotropic null, WT - mutant P(6) delta = -0.133 vs +0.18, PCP nematic order 0.955 vs 0.9, bond-tensor isotropic residual c0 = -0.025 vs 0. Deductions: four of the six new references are approximate figure reads recorded offline (flagged in the JSON `provenance` fields) rather than digitised values (-6); the Classen (2005) comparison fails in sign and is reported, not resolved (-5); the oriented-T1 reference is a null model rather than a measured Aigouy/Etournay orientation distribution (-2); the Lewis's-law r = 0.9994 of measurement 5 is inflated by the L401-405 reweighting (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py L1765–L1771: pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta = -0.133 against reference +0.18: sign mismatch with Classen et al. (2005) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py#L1765-L1771>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-euler-mean-polygon-side-number>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-laser-ablation-initial-recoil-velocity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-lewis-law-area-topology-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-bond-tensor-isotropic-residual>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-hinge-cell-elongation-peak-q>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-hinge-rearrangement-shear-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-nematic-order-parameter-final>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-oriented-t1-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pcp-wt-minus-mutant-hexagonal-fraction-delta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pupal-vs-larval-topological-disorder-ratio-mu2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-pupal-wing-annealed-hexagonal-fraction-p6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-specimen-segmented-polygon-distribution-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-wing-disc-polygon-distribution-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-measurement-wing-disc-proliferating-hexagonal-fraction-p6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — MorphoEval overall 84.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py` (84.8/100, down from 90.9 in Pass 2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: Section 2b adds a genuine vertex model (tri-cellular vertices, analytic forces of Farhadifar Eq. 1 verified by finite differences, T1 exchanges) coupled to an explicit per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor with zero trace and perpendicular cancellation (Lean theorem 5), driven by a pupal hinge-contraction pure-shear strain with an Etournay-style shear decomposition (Lean theorem 6). At eps_pcp = 0.5 the model gives a cell-elongation peak <|Q|> = 0.253 (Etournay 2015 ~0.25, approx.), 20 T1s all on AP-oriented junctions versus 11 in the eps_pcp = 0 control, a rearrangement share of tissue shear of 0.307 (vs 0.165 control), bond-tension anisotropy Lambda_AP/Lambda_PD = 2.39 and a monotonic eps_pcp sweep. The re-score is lower because the audit now records what the v2 scores overlooked: the Section 2 regimes are Lloyd relaxations whose Lewis's-law fit is imposed by a post-hoc area reweighting, the only vendored specimen is a mouse epithelium, three new DOIs and all new reference values are unverified offline, and the PCP effect on hexagon fraction has the opposite sign to Classen et al. (2005). Overall 84.8/100 (faithfulness 83.1, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py at 7e4f207, image/png, 1297705 B, 3075×1935 px, artifact_sha256 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7 (sha256 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7), spec_fingerprint 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52; artifact_sha256: 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse). | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78, and PCP (fz, stbm) mutants fail to reach wild-type hexagonal order. | Aigouy et al. (2010) Cell & Etournay et al. (2015) eLife: hinge contraction from ~15 hAPF stretches the blade along the proximal-distal axis, cells elongate along PD and then relax through oriented cell rearrangements while the Fz/Stbm PCP axis reorients to PD; tissue shear decomposes into cell-elongation change plus rearrangement, division and correlation contributions.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic Voronoi-seed (Lloyd-type) packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep (Section 2, panels A1-A4, B1-B5). | Pass 3: explicit tri-cellular vertex model (analytic forces of Eq. 1, T1 exchanges) on a 100-cell patch with a per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor Q_ab modulating line tension Lambda_ab = Lambda_bar (1 + eps_pcp n.Q_ab.n), Fz-Stbm feedback + flow-alignment polarity dynamics, an area-preserving hinge-contraction boundary strain diag(lambda, 1/lambda) with ln lambda = 0.35, shear decomposition into cell-elongation and rearrangement parts, a PCP loss-of-function (eps_pcp = 0) control and a 6-point eps_pcp sweep (Section 2b, panels C1-C5, GIF panel 4). | Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the vendored apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913 against the Farhadifar wing-disc distribution).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells. | The vendored specimen `drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg` is a Wikimedia Commons epithelial monolayer whose scout manifest records organism Mus musculus; its polygon statistics are compared with Drosophila literature values as a cross-species epithelial-packing transfer, not as a Drosophila specimen. | The Section 2 regimes are Voronoi-seed relaxations with a post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting and a hexagonal-lattice pull in the pupal regime; only Section 2b integrates the Farhadifar energy on vertex degrees of freedom. | The PCP coupling sign (PCP-complex-bearing AP junctions stiffened for eps_pcp > 0), the polarity-dynamics gains (k_fb = 0.6, k_flow = 0.4), the initial polarity spread (0.6 rad) and the hinge log-strain (0.35) are modelling choices, not fitted to data; Pass 3 reference values from Etournay (2015) and Classen (2005) are approximate figure reads recorded offline.; does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature, 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions, Fat/Dachsous polarity, the pre-15 hAPF margin-directed PCP pattern, cell divisions or extrusions during pupal morphogenesis, the hinge as a separate mechanical compartment, or periodic boundary conditions for the explicit vertex model (the patch is clamped at its margin). | Does not claim to reproduce the Classen et al. (2005) PCP-mutant loss of hexagonal order: in this model the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (sign mismatch disclosed in measurement `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:1765-1771 and 774-1023 — the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (P(6) 0.867 -> 0.733 for eps_pcp 0 -> 0.5) whereas Classen et al. (2005) report the opposite; add the PCP-dependent junction remodeling/annealing step (post-T1 junction regrowth and polarity-dependent tension relaxation) and a longer post-contraction relaxation window, then re-test the sign of `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:401-405 and 378-379 — remove the post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting (`adjusted_areas = areas * (1 + 0.14 * gamma_slope_boost * (n - 6))`) and the hexagonal-lattice pull (`0.042 * hex_disp`) from `simulate_vertex_regime`, and re-derive panels A1-A4 / measurements 1-7 from the Section 2b explicit vertex model (periodic version with division) so Lewis's law and pupal hexagonal order are emergent rather than imposed.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:533-567 and 846-848 — replace the clamped non-periodic patch by a periodic explicit vertex model with an affine box deformation so boundary cells participate in the mechanics, and add the Sugimura & Ishihara (2013) force-inference tension anisotropy as a quantitative comparison for `tension_anisotropy_ratio`.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py:782-785, 931 and 523-524 — expose k_feedback, k_flow, init_polarity_sigma and the T1 thresholds on the CLI, cite or fit them (Aigouy 2010 polarity-alignment time scale; Farhadifar 2007 l_T1), and render the hinge-strain sweep (gamma_PD in [0, 0.5]) as a panel rather than leaving it in development notes.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_reference.json:192-252 — the Etournay (2015) |Q| peak 0.25 and ~0.5 rearrangement share, the Classen (2005) 0.78 / 0.60 hexagon fractions and the three new DOIs are offline figure reads; digitise the Etournay Fig. 3 shear curves and the Classen polygon histograms into a pinned table, resolve the DOIs, and replace the `provenance: approximate` flags.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/scout_manifest.json:8 and drosophila_wing_vertex_model_reference.json:54-62 — the vendored specimen is a Mus musculus epithelium; vendor a genuine Drosophila pupal-wing or wing-disc micrograph (e.g. a CC-BY panel from Etournay et al. 2015 eLife or Aigouy et al. 2010 if licence permits), pin its SHA-256, segment it, and record the species consistently in JSON, README and file name." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.48e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 adds a 6-point eps_pcp sweep (-0.6 .. 0.8, L1026-1061, panel C5) that is monotonic in T1 count (5 -> 29), rearrangement share (0.06 -> 0.43), residual elongation (0.295 -> 0.166) and bond-tension anisotropy (0.31 -> 4.1), with eps_pcp = 0 as the loss-of-function control; `--pcp-epsilon` and `--hinge-strain` are wired through the CLI (L2004-2015, L2027-2034) and the hinge strain controls the elongation peak (0.13 at gamma = 0, 0.31 at gamma = 0.5 in the Pass 3 diagnostics). The Pass 2 7-point Lambda_bar sweep and (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase map are retained. Deductions: hinge strain is swept only in the development notes, not rendered (-4); k_fb, k_flow and the initial polarity spread are not exposed on the CLI (-3); the P(6) response to eps_pcp is monotonic but in the biologically wrong direction, so the parameter controls the feature without matching its sign (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Reproducibility package: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seeds (2007 for Section 2, 2007 + 43 for Section 2b), `--self-test` passes 14 checks in ~6 s including the SHA-256 gate, a central-difference check of the analytic vertex forces, PCP tensor identities, T1 bookkeeping and two-run bitwise determinism of the vertex model (L1848-1973); the default render takes ~17 s and regenerates both artifacts; all CLI flags are documented in argparse. Deductions: no requirements lock file in this slot (environment recorded only in this audit) (-4); the self-test and measurements re-run the vertex model with different step counts (500 vs 900), so the measured values are not the self-tested ones (-3); matplotlib emits a cache-directory warning unless MPLCONFIGDIR is set, which the invocation notes do not mention (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Source and data traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The five Pass 2 DOIs are retained; the dataset README, bib and JSON gain Aigouy (2010), Etournay (2015) and Sugimura & Ishihara (2013) with explicit \"recorded offline, not re-verified online\" flags (README L29-39, bib L55-91, JSON L32-52); the specimen SHA-256 is unchanged and verified fail-closed at runtime (L96-115); the JSON records the exact PCP model statement and defaults (L192-215). Deductions: three DOIs could not be resolved in this pass (-5); the numeric Pass 3 reference values are unlocated beyond figure-level loci and carry no digitisation (-5); the specimen's species is recorded inconsistently (\"Mus musculus\" in the scout manifest, unspecified in the JSON, \"Drosophila wing\" in the file name) (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the regenerated PNG: the four Section 2 regimes are visually distinct, the segmentation overlay (A5) follows the junction network of the micrograph, and the new C1/C2 panels show PD-elongated cells with bonds coloured by PCP-modulated tension against an isotropic control, which resembles the elongated pupal blade cells of Aigouy et al. (2010) qualitatively. Deductions: the only vendored specimen is a Wikimedia epithelium whose own scout manifest records organism Mus musculus (scout_manifest.json:8) and whose JSON entry gives no species (reference JSON L54-62), so the r = 0.9913 P(n) agreement is a cross-species transfer and not a Drosophila wing match (-12); no Drosophila wing-disc or pupal-wing image (e.g. a CC-BY eLife panel from Etournay 2015) is placed side by side with the simulation, so the hinge-contraction morphology is validated only against approximate numbers (-6); the explicit vertex patch is only 100 cells with a clamped margin, visibly smaller than the ~10^4-cell blade (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/scout_manifest.json L8–L8: Scout manifest records organism 'Mus musculus' for the vendored micrograph — not a Drosophila specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/datasets/drosophila_wing_vertex_model/scout_manifest.json#L8-L8>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

